    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "You can combine the solution from the previous question you asked about 'mini.statusline' (#1579) with `:h wordcount()`.\r\n\r\nThe solution is to create a separate section that uses `vim.fn.wordcount().words` to show the number of words in the current buffer. The number of characters would be `chars` field. Use this to create a separate section and put it in whatever place feels best by following [the accepted solution](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1579#discussioncomment-12228934).",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">You can combine the solution from the previous question you asked about 'mini.statusline' (<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"7981855\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1579\" data-hovercard-type=\"discussion\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1579/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1579\">#1579</a>) with <code class=\"notranslate\">:h wordcount()</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The solution is to create a separate section that uses <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.fn.wordcount().words</code> to show the number of words in the current buffer. The number of characters would be <code class=\"notranslate\">chars</code> field. Use this to create a separate section and put it in whatever place feels best by following <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1579#discussioncomment-12228934\" data-hovercard-type=\"discussion\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1579/hovercard?comment_id=12228934\">the accepted solution</a>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "You can combine the solution from the previous question you asked about 'mini.statusline' (#1579) with :h wordcount().\nThe solution is to create a separate section that uses vim.fn.wordcount().words to show the number of words in the current buffer. The number of characters would be chars field. Use this to create a separate section and put it in whatever place feels best by following the accepted solution.",
